<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>dev.wingmen.sre-lane-recycle</string>

  <!-- The RED half of fleet auto-recycle-at-80% (operator: hands-off, no babysitting).
       Runs sre_lane_recycle.py: discovers running worker lanes, computes gates
       (idle + git_clean + fresh_handoff [CAI-681 floor] + context_bloat>=80% [my
       trigger]) and, WHEN ARMED, recycles only the genuinely-bloated ones.

       RECONCILED 2026-10-02 (cc-fleet-health, orch-console #49586): this file had
       drifted from the actually-running job (an untracked hand-edit in
       ~/Library/LaunchAgents) AND its own comment was stale. Corrections:
       1. The code's arm-bit (CAI-681 cond 5) has been STANDING-ARMED BY DEFAULT
          since CAI-RESP-1382 (cai ruled the post-director-demo precondition was
          met >1mo prior) — a bare invocation with NO flag now runs ARMED, the
          OPPOSITE of what this file's old comment ("no --arm => detect-only")
          claimed. --no-arm below is now REQUIRED to stay detect-only; it is not
          optional decoration. The "CAI-700 two-task control" this file used to
          cite is a DIFFERENT, unrelated decision (the lane_tasks auto-drain
          pipeline, CAI-RESP-700) — not a gate on this mechanism at all.
       2. Still genuinely NOT safe to arm, for two separate reasons (unrelated to
          CAI-700): (a) Gap-1 — gate_context_bloat still approximates every
          lane's window as 1M tokens; no canonical per-lane pct yet (see
          sre_lane_recycle.py's own inline TODO). (b) the amber-checkpoint dedup
          gap (memory ctx-health-amber-nudge-dedup-backlog) means a lane's
          handoff can go stale for weeks while the nudge keeps firing — observed
          live on cc-irsyad-coord (handoff untouched since Aug 20 despite daily
          amber nudges). Neither is proven fixed; do not arm fleet-wide on the
          strength of this reconciliation alone.
       3. The LIVE copy (~/Library/LaunchAgents, hand-edited, untracked) was found
          CRASH-LOOPING on every single 300s invocation (ModuleNotFoundError:
          nervous_system — missing PYTHONPATH) — meaning detect-only coverage was
          providing ZERO visibility, not just "disarmed." Fixed live + mirrored
          the fix here. This explains the Musa cosem-port-at-1%-context miss.

       TO ARM (only after Gap-1 + the dedup gap are closed and reported to cai):
       remove --no-arm below (the boundary + CTX_WD_LANE_ARM still fail-closed
       independently). Singletons (hub/cai/Nazim/SRE) are structurally excluded
       in code — never recyclable here.

       Pairs with dev.wingmen.context-health-watchdog (--arm=amber, the WRITE-ONLY
       checkpoint that PRODUCES the fresh handoffs this half gates on). -->

  <key>ProgramArguments</key><array>
    <string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/.venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/scripts/sre_lane_recycle.py</string>
    <string>--no-arm</string>
    <!-- REQUIRED to stay detect-only — the code defaults to ARMED since CAI-RESP-1382. -->
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator</string>

  <!-- Matches the actually-running cadence/scope (reconciled, not a new decision):
       worker-lanes-first staged exclusion (Nazim #37793) stays as-is here — dropping
       any prefix from it is orch-console's governance call, not reconciled by this edit. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>300</integer>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key><dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa</string>
    <key>PYTHONPATH</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator</string>
    <key>SRE_LANE_EXCLUDE_PREFIXES</key><string>cc-irsyad,cc-cosem,cc-shipforge,cc-storefront</string>
    <!-- Trigger threshold overridable: CTX_WD_HARD (0.80), CONSOLE_CTX_WINDOW (1M).
         The ARM switch is CTX_WD_LANE_ARM=1 (or dropping --no-arm) — NOT set here. -->
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/sre-lane-recycle.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/sre-lane-recycle.out.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
